            <div xml:id="d451">

                <pb facs="0791" n="721" sameAs="frus:frus1883/pg721"/>

                <head>No. 452.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Phelps to Mr.
                    Frelinghuysen.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Lima</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1883-10-04"
                                ><hi rendition="#italic">October</hi> 4, 1883</date>. (Received
                        October 27.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 11.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: An order appeared yesterday announcing that
                    Lima would be evacuated on the 20th instant, and Callao, with its custom-house,
                    on the 21st, the Chilians surrendering the two cities to General Iglesias and
                    retiring to neighboring localities.</p>
                <p>Very respectfully, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>S. L. PHELPS.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
